       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day, which is about 7 times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A dose that high risks severe hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function. It's also far above the 10 g or 150 mg/kg single-dose range where toxicity becomes a concern, and for a 70 kg patient that threshold is about 10 g.\n\nI suspect it's a typo for **1,000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day). That's a standard dose, and it falls within the 4 g/day maximum. If so, I can enter it right away.\n\nPlease confirm one of these:\n- **1,000 mg PO TID**, which is the likely intent.\n- **650 mg PO q6h** or another regimen you prefer.\n- If you really do intend 10,000 mg, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still want to hear that before entering it."
