       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A single 10,000 mg dose of acetaminophen is in the range that can cause serious liver injury in a 70 kg adult. Three of those doses in a day (30 g) could be life-threatening. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical rationale, and I can't think of a scenario where this dose is therapeutic.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 1,000 mg PO TID** (3 g/day), or **1,000 mg PO q6h** (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- **Enter another regimen** within safe limits if you tell me what you want.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this dose is intentional, they can review it. The system will probably require that review anyway.\n\nIf a patient has already received a dose like this, or an overdose is suspected, please contact poison control and start the acetaminophen toxicity protocol (NAC) right away.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
